/*  FUNCTION NAME:      THUNK
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Wraps a value in a zero-argument lambda (a "thunk") so it is returned only when the result is called with ().*/
/*  RETURNS:            LAMBDA: a zero-argument function that returns x when called with ()
    PARAMETERS:
        x               (Required) The value to defer. Captured by closure and returned when the thunk is called.
    EXAMPLE:            =THUNK(42)() -> 42 (call the thunk with () to retrieve the value; =THUNK(42) on its own returns a function, shown as #CALC!)
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-06-17  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
THUNK = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [x],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        result, LAMBDA(x),
        result
)
);
